More than 100 Israeli settlers stormed a village in the occupied West Bank early on Tuesday, setting fire to Palestinian properties and wounding three members of Israel's security forces. The raid, which drew rare government condemnation, came as the military attempted to accompany a Palestinian family back to their home after they had been displaced by earlier settler attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d947c52-bbf1-11f1-91bc-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/0118268afa52a94c8110d9ec5c3e1f3d1420de20.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d947c52-bbf1-11f1-91bc-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/0118268afa52a94c8110d9ec5c3e1f3d1420de20.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e66ce8c-bbf1-11f1-a2c6-21fb1f6856f3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:35:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d947c52-bbf1-11f1-91bc-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/0118268afa52a94c8110d9ec5c3e1f3d1420de20.jpg">© Zain Jaafar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Video shows Iranian police beating, sexually humiliating teenage detainee</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-police-video-teenage-detainee-abuse</link><description>
A video posted in mid-September showing Iranian police officers beating and sexually harassing an arrested teenage boy has caused widespread outrage in Iran. Experts say such mistreatment of people accused of common crimes is frequent in Iran, but the footage provides rare visual evidence of what they describe as a recurring practice within the police force.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a691568-b8ea-11f1-8115-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-25-at-4-06-05-PM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a691568-b8ea-11f1-8115-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-25-at-4-06-05-PM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">92aee040-bbe4-11f1-8f24-1f6053ff47a2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:56:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a691568-b8ea-11f1-8115-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-25-at-4-06-05-PM.png">© Les Observateurs</source><dc:creator>Ershad ALIJANI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran says it expects US response Tuesday on plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-says-expects-us-response-tuesday-plan-reopen-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said Tehran expects Washington to respond to its proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz on Tuesday. In exchange for reopening the vital shipping route, Tehran is seeking guarantees including a regional ceasefire, the lifting of sanctions on its oil sector and an end to the US naval blockade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc1d708-bbca-11f1-b635-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268737302690.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc1d708-bbca-11f1-b635-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268737302690.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eeedbab0-bbcc-11f1-8750-c5eb01e184f1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:32:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc1d708-bbca-11f1-b635-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268737302690.jpg">© Yuki Iwamura, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Trump 'flips & flops' with Iran between making a deal and threats to attack in ‘devastating fashion’]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260928-saudis-furious-trump-flips-flops-between-deal-with-iran-and-attacks-in-devastating-fashion</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Stimson Center. She describes the US-Iran conflict as a dangerous combination of military escalation, diplomatic ambiguity and political calculation. Slavin sees an absence of true diplomacy: the recent indirect contacts between Washington and Tehran, mediated by Qatar, have been too limited and too fragile to produce any serious breakthrough. For her, this amounts to "kabuki diplomacy": they half engage while positioning themselves against any appearance of compromise.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/770340f4-bc0a-11f1-8dc6-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6026989696abbbe576b3cc4-31536915.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/770340f4-bc0a-11f1-8dc6-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6026989696abbbe576b3cc4-31536915.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d973d0c0-bb68-11f1-8748-9145122832b6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:18:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump expects Iran talks next week after rejecting seven-day truce proposal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-trump-expects-iran-talks-next-week-after-rejecting-seven-day-truce-proposal</link><description>
